    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes `POST /api/owners` (and the owner responses generally) return a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo edits, following the project's OpenAPI-generated-DTO + MapStruct conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nSince the mapper is used by both the create and read paths, the field is populated consistently. `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
